WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.850
Speaker 1: We have to start today with something
so important and of such consequence, but

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:11.450
which regularly generates almost no interest
from our audience, which is foreign policy

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:16.090
and what's going on right now with Russia
and Ukraine, as we've been covering and as

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:21.619
many of you have been seeing on a variety
of different media outlets.

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:25.050
Russia has been massing troops at the border
with Ukraine.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:32.739
Now, even that statement is questioned by
some who want to defend Putin or claim that

00:00:32.739 --> 00:00:37.370
that's all a lie for the purposes of furthering
American imperialism or whatever.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:43.129
We're going to have a real hard time having
any conversation if we can't even agree on

00:00:43.129 --> 00:00:46.309
the fundamentals, but that's going on.

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:51.839
And now the discussion is among the United
States, as well as other Naito allies about

00:00:51.839 --> 00:00:59.250
if, when and how to mobilize military resources
to NATO's allies surrounding Ukraine.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.629
Remembering that Ukraine is not part of NATO's.

00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:08.229
And that's a piece of this as well, with the
question of what would happen with those troops

00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:14.250
if indeed Russia did push into Ukraine and
what would be Russia's reason for doing so.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:18.890
When does Vladimir Putin really plan to do
that, or is he only making it appear as though

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.420
he might plan to do that?

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:25.730
So the latest news is that the Pentagon has
put 8500 troops on what they are calling heightened

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:32.479
alert, and that Joe Biden was presented with
a number of options, including moving troops

00:01:32.479 --> 00:01:37.759
and equipment from other parts of Europe into
Poland, Romania and other neighboring countries

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:38.759
to Ukraine.

00:01:38.759 --> 00:01:43.869
Again, remembering that Ukraine itself is
not a NATO's ally, the U.S. is discussing

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:48.230
the deployment of military forces to Eastern
Europe with Naito allies.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:53.549
Lloyd Austin has played it placed 8500 troops
on heightened alert to assist with the defense

00:01:53.549 --> 00:01:55.259
of Naito allies.

00:01:55.259 --> 00:01:57.110
We have a clip of that.

00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:00.610
Here is John Kirby, the spokesperson from
the Pentagon.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:04.619
Speaker 2: I want to provide some facts on
these preparations that will reinforce our

00:02:04.619 --> 00:02:10.119
commitment to NADO and to the NATO's response
force and increase our readiness.

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:14.950
Secretary Austin has placed a range of units
in the United States on a heightened preparedness

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:20.340
to deploy, which increases our readiness to
provide forces if NATO's should activate the

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.170
NEF or if other situations develop.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:31.310
All told, the number of forces that the secretary
has placed on heightened alert comes up to

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:36.980
about 8500 personnel,
Speaker 1: so we don't know what's going to

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:37.980
happen yet.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:42.150
There are all sorts of different speculations,
which quite frankly, aren't super interesting

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:45.739
to me because we just don't know what Vladimir
Putin is thinking.

00:02:45.739 --> 00:02:49.620
But one of the most interesting aspects of
this is how different political factions in

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.460
the U.S. have responded.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:03:00.790
As many of you now probably know on the Trump
right, there is indeed a pro-Putin pro-Russia

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:04.849
wing which developed under Trump.

00:03:04.849 --> 00:03:10.879
And it came in part from Trump's sort of deference
to Vladimir Putin for lack of a better term.

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:16.269
Not saying Putin is a puppet master of Trump
in any direct way.

00:03:16.269 --> 00:03:20.989
I'm not saying they colluded together to figure
you don't have to believe any of that stuff.

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:22.690
That's not what I'm saying.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:26.299
Trump has been enamored with strongman, authoritarian
dictator types.

00:03:26.299 --> 00:03:28.680
He talked about how he and Kim Jong UN fell
in love.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.189
I might even have that clip.

00:03:30.189 --> 00:03:32.980
We fell in love,
Speaker 2: and then we fell in love.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:33.980
Exactly.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.560
Speaker 1: You guys know all this stuff.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:43.439
And to that end, we have seen a lot of these
Trumpists kind of become enamored similarly

00:03:43.439 --> 00:03:45.770
with Putin and Russia.

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:51.280
Similarly, there are some on the left what
I tend to call.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.280
Here we go.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:58.519
The revolutionary left, the Stalinist Leninist
left, and that's lenahan.

00:03:58.519 --> 00:04:01.329
By the way, some of you write to me and spell
Lenin like John Lennon.

00:04:01.329 --> 00:04:02.840
And I'm wondering, like, who do these?

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:06.370
Who do they think I'm referring to when I
say Leninist anyway?

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:12.299
There are some there as well who have become
very deferential to Russia.

00:04:12.299 --> 00:04:16.360
Usually they are sort of pro Chavez Maduro
types.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.850
Often they like Fidel Castro.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:22.830
Sometimes their views on Syria are sort of
strange.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.360
So there's that group as well.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:28.510
But one of the really interesting things is
that there's kind of a factual firewall that

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:36.290
seems to be plaguing some where yesterday
I saw, for example, why is it that Tucker

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:40.930
saying we should be loyal to Russia is not
OK?

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:45.200
But Democrats saying we should be loyal to
Ukraine is OK.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.000
Like, either way, you're just kind of picking
a side.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:52.340
And of course, I'm not picking any sides.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:59.450
I'm against aggression and I'm against strongman
authoritarians in this particular.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:05.950
Case, it's Putin massing the troops at the
border with Ukraine, it is not Ukraine massing

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:11.510
troops at the border with Russia and throwing
signals as if they might invade Russia.

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:15.920
So you can have any analysis that makes sense
to you.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:19.970
You can have a particular predilection for
Russia or Ukraine.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:22.540
And quite frankly, I don't.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:28.150
But to say it's sort of the same when one
side clearly is the one at least feigning

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:34.810
aggression, if not actually planning to carry
it out is not a very sensible analysis.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.750
So now there's going to be some wait and see.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:43.620
And if anybody is going to write in and say,
David, you imperialist bastard wanting us,

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:46.310
I don't want any aggression.

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.340
I don't want any invasion.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:50.100
I don't want any war.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.870
I don't want troop deployment.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:52.870
I don't.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:53.870
I don't want any of it.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:57.620
I think it's all bad and and I'm selfishly
of that opinion.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:00.490
I want stable economies.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:04.061
What's happening in the stock market almost
daily is not pleasing to me, and I think it

00:06:04.061 --> 00:06:06.370
would only get worse if these escalations
were so.

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:07.460
I'm against all of it.

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:10.930
I don't want the U.S. invading anybody or
anything like that.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:15.740
Now, once you understand the dynamics of Ukraine
not even being in NATO and the discussion

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:21.210
with Biden and NATO's allies is about the
defense of NATO's allies in the area.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:25.210
You understand that that conversation isn't
even the appropriate one to be having, but

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.830
that's what's going on.

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:29.210
We may know more within a day.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:48.370
We may know more within weeks could be months.

00:06:48.370 --> 00:07:29.370
We just don't know.

